orm a strong Open 4 if connected at I7, and the diagonal segment H10-I9-J8), the opponent (White) has a much more immediate and lethal threat.\n\nWhite has established four consecutive stones in Row 9 at coordinates E9, F9, G9, and H9. This formation is blocked on the right side by Black\'s stone at I9, but it is completely open on the left side at D9. This is known as a "Four" or "Rush 4".\n\nReason: In Gomoku, a "Four" with an open end is an immediate game-ending threat. If Black does not block the open end at D9 on this turn, White will play at D9 on their next turn to complete a 5-in-a-row (D9-E9-F9-G9-H9) and win the game. No other offensive move by Black can be executed fast enough to counter this threat, as White\'s win would occur on the very next move. Therefore, Black is forced to play defensively at D9 to block the line and prolong the game.\n\nAnswer: {"col": "D", "row": 9}'}
